https://lrclib.net/api/get?artist_name={artist}&track_name={track}&album_name={album}&duration={duration}

Match the returned track against:

- Artist.
- Track title.
- Album.
- Duration.

Do not display mismatched lyrics.

# 7. AUDIO SOURCE RESOLUTION

Implement a dedicated AudioSourceResolver.

The resolver must operate independently from metadata search.

Resolution process:

STEP 1 — Identify the requested recording.

Extract:

- Track title.
- Primary artist.
- Featured artists.
- Album.
- Duration.
- Recording identifiers when available.

STEP 2 — Search authorized sources.

Audius should be searched first when appropriate.

Compare:

- Title similarity.
- Artist similarity.
- Duration.
- Recording identity.

Do not automatically choose the first result.

STEP 3 — Validate the candidate.

Check:

- Provider availability.
- Whether playback is authorized.
- Whether the stream is accessible.
- Whether the track is complete.
- Whether the source is actually audio.
- Whether the recording matches the requested track.

STEP 4 — Select the best valid source.

STEP 5 — Start playback.

STEP 6 — If playback fails, attempt the next eligible provider.

STEP 7 — If no valid source exists, show a clear unavailable state.

Never silently substitute an unrelated remix, cover, live performance, or another artist's recording.

Create a source status badge:

- Audius
- Official Embed
- Preview
- Unavailable

Use accurate labels.

Never display FULL TRACK unless the provider confirms the complete recording is available.

Persist source preferences locally, but revalidate availability before playback.

